10:["$","section",null,{"className":"paper-section","id":"method","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Method overview"}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"paper-figure architecture-figure","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/remm/figures/architecture-full-transparent.png","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","aria-label":"Enlarge the robot execution architecture","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/remm/figures/architecture-full-transparent.png","width":"1909","height":"854","alt":"Observations and task instructions enter REMM, which sends an atomic instruction to the frozen G0.5 executor and Galaxea R1 Lite robot."}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"The execution loop."}]," REMM selects the atomic instruction ",["$","$L16",null,{"term":"c"}],"; the frozen ",["$","a",null,{"className":"reference-link","href":"https://opengalaxea.github.io/G05/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":"G0.5"}]," policy executes it with native visual and robot-state inputs."]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"prose intro","children":["REMM maintains ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"task state outside the policy"}],". Visual evidence updates memory; the supervisor selects the next nominal or recovery skill. The active instruction ",["$","$L16",null,{"term":"c"}]," stays fixed until a ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"verified skill boundary"}],"."]}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"paper-figure architecture-detail","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/remm/figures/architecture-memory-transparent-v3.png","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","aria-label":"Enlarge REMM internal architecture","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/remm/figures/architecture-memory-transparent-v3.png","width":"1898","height":"1334","loading":"lazy","alt":"REMM internals: task decomposition and skill contracts, source-specific evidence gates, event ledger, assertion records, support graph, dependency invalidation, and recovery scheduling."}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Inside REMM."}]," Task, evidence, and memory revision connect accepted observations to a revised skill queue. Select either diagram to enlarge it."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"notation-equation","aria-label":"Memory consists of ledger, assertion records, support graph, and skill queue","children":[["$","$L16",null,{"term":"M"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"= ("}],["$","$L16",null,{"term":"L"}],["$","span",null,{"children":","}],["$","$L16",null,{"term":"F"}],["$","span",null,{"children":","}],["$","$L16",null,{"term":"D"}],["$","span",null,{"children":","}],["$","$L16",null,{"term":"Q"}],["$","span",null,{"children":")"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"notation-hint","children":"Hover, focus, or tap a symbol for its meaning."}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"method-equation","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Memory selects an instruction; the frozen policy acts"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"equation-lines","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","$L16",null,{"term":"c"}]," = ",["$","span",null,{"className":"math-word","children":"active"}],"(",["$","$L16",null,{"term":"Q"}],")"]}],["$","div",null,{"children":["(",["$","i",null,{"children":"y"}],["$","sub",null,{"children":"τ"}],", Â",["$","sub",null,{"children":"τ"}],["$","sup",null,{"children":"1:J"}],") = π",["$","sub",null,{"children":"G0.5"}],"(",["$","$L16",null,{"term":"observations"}],", ",["$","$L16",null,{"term":"c"}],", ",["$","i",null,{"children":"e"}],["$","sub",null,{"children":"R1"}],"; ",["$","$L16",null,{"term":"weights"}],")"]}],["$","small",null,{"className":"math-key","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"children":"y"}],["$","sub",null,{"children":"τ"}],": optional reasoning tokens"]}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"math-vector","children":"Â"}],["$","sub",null,{"children":"τ"}],["$","sup",null,{"children":"1:J"}],": action chunk"]}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"children":"J"}],": chunk length"]}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","i",null,{"children":"e"}],["$","sub",null,{"children":"R1"}],": robot embodiment identifier"]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"equation-example","children":["REMM dispatches one atomic instruction, such as “Place the blue block in the bowl.” G0.5 receives that text with its native observations and embodiment identifier. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"The memory database stays outside the policy."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"prose method-text","children":["$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a"]}]]}]
11:["$","figure",null,{"className":"teaser paper-figure","children":[["$","img",null,{"src":"/remm/figures/teaser-transparent-e59fe15d.png","width":"1919","height":"935","alt":"Illustrative comparison: a disturbed completed condition remains stale without revision, while REMM schedules a repair."}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Revising a completed condition."}]," The paper’s teaser illustrates how a disturbance can invalidate earlier task progress and lead to a targeted repair. This is a qualitative example, not an aggregate result."]}]]}]
12:[["$","section",null,{"className":"paper-section","id":"tasks","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Physical experiments"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"prose","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":["We evaluate REMM in ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"51 physical trials"}]," on ",["$","a",null,{"className":"reference-link","href":"https://docs.galaxea-ai.com/Guide/R1Lite/R1Lite_Hardware_Introduction/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":"Galaxea R1 Lite"}],". All three systems use the frozen G0.5 executor: Vanilla G0.5 without external memory, a memory-enabled adaptation of ",["$","a",null,{"className":"reference-link","href":"https://happywaterxp.github.io/HiMe/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":"HiMe"}],", and REMM. The comparison measures the complete deployed systems; the memory baseline is a controlled adaptation, not an official reproduction."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"T1 and disturbed T2 probe revision; nominal T2 and T3 probe retention and grounding, rather than directly testing dependency propagation. The tasks separate three questions: can a controller revise a previously satisfied condition, retain information that is no longer visible, and turn that information into the correct next instruction?"}]]}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"paper-figure task-figure","children":[["$","img",null,{"src":"/remm/figures/setup-transparent.png","width":"1918","height":"1688","loading":"lazy","alt":"Physical task sequences for T1a, T1b, T2, and T3. Orange borders identify robot execution and blue borders identify human motion."}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Physical evaluation setups."}]," T1a tests recovery with queued work; T1b tests a changed recovery destination. T2 tests order memory and disturbed execution; T3 tests hidden-object identity."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"prose task-list","children":[["$","article",null,{"data-task":"T1","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"T1a · Recovery with queued work"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"After a relevant placement and full arm retraction, a human moves the designated object out of its container while unrelated work remains queued. The controller must revise the affected completed condition and schedule a bounded repair without interrupting the active skill."}]]}],["$","article",null,{"data-task":"T1","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"T1b · Destination changes after pouring"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Exactly one designated residual object remains in the bowl after pouring and retraction. Its required final destination is the green tray. Later accepted evidence must revise stale completion and resolve the pending recovery against the current destination."}]]}],["$","article",null,{"data-task":"T2","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"T2 · Ordered recall and disturbed repeats"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Three colored cues are introduced sequentially and then covered. The robot must match their remembered order to current objects and execute the placements in sequence. Predeclared disturbed repeats relocate a pending or already placed target, testing repair without losing the remaining order. A delayed-recall variant inserts two unrelated placements before ordered retrieval."}]]}],["$","article",null,{"data-task":"T3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"T3 · Hidden-object rearrangement"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The robot observes an object–cup binding and must retain the cover’s identity through a shuffle before selecting the cup to lift. The controlled physical protocol moves one cup at a time with pauses; faster or fully overlapping shuffles are a different observability condition."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","$L1b",null,{}],["$","section",null,{"className":"paper-section","id":"results","children":["$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22"]}],"$L23"]
13:["$","section",null,{"className":"paper-section prose","id":"appendix","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Technical appendix"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Inspect JSON records, step through memory revision, and follow the references from visual evidence to a recovery instruction."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"appendix-link","children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/remm/appendix/","children":"Read the technical appendix →"}]}]]}]
14:["$","section",null,{"className":"paper-section prose status","id":"limitations","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Scope and limitations"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"REMM uses compiler-supplied dependencies, conservative 2D perception, and boundary-only repair. The physical study uses one robot and controlled tabletop interventions. The generated clips isolate memory readout and grounding, not physical task completion. Pooled outcomes include assisted runs and incomplete labels; they do not establish unassisted autonomy or isolate dependency propagation. Offline T3 uses a specialized tracker. Broader testing is needed for unconstrained occlusion, appearance shift, new task semantics, and other robots."}]]}]
15:["$","footer",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"REMM · Revisable Embodied Memory for Manipulation"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"#overview","children":"Back to top ↑"}]]}]
