18:["$","p",null,{"children":["Accepted evidence updates ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"current object relations"}]," in ",["$","$L16",null,{"term":"S"}]," while preserving the event history in ",["$","$L16",null,{"term":"L"}],". Assertion records ",["$","$L16",null,{"term":"F"}]," retain their support links in ",["$","$L16",null,{"term":"D"}],". When a supporting fact becomes inactive, ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"dependent conclusions are invalidated"}],". An object’s inferred location, for example, loses support when the containment relation no longer holds."]}]
19:["$","h3",null,{"children":"Recovery and verification"}]
1a:["$","p",null,{"children":["A broken completed goal creates or updates a repair skill ",["$","$L16",null,{"term":"rho"}],". A relevant disturbance schedules repair after the active skill; unrelated recovery can wait until the remaining nominal work in ",["$","$L16",null,{"term":"Q"}]," is complete. A pending repair may ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"change destination as new evidence arrives"}],". Visual outcome checks determine whether the supervisor advances, retries, or pauses for review."]}]
1c:["$","h2",null,{"children":"Physical results"}]
1d:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["REMM has ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"10 of 17 trials recorded as full completion"}],", compared with 2 of 16 for HiMe and 0 of 18 for Vanilla G0.5. Seven REMM trials remain partial; none is labeled a complete failure. These pooled counts are descriptive because the task mix and sample sizes differ. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"They include operator-assisted trials and are not unassisted-autonomy success rates."}]," Two REMM full completions have task assistance recorded."]}]}]
1e:["$","details",null,{"className":"result-details","children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":"Baseline adaptation and assistance accounting"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"prose","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"The local HiMe adaptation retains planner/sentry roles, episodic and procedural stores, and add/update/delete operations. Its configured planner and sentry use Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct, MiniLM-L6-v2 retrieval, and an eight-frame working context, with task prompts and instruction parsing adapted to G0.5. It is not a reproduction of the original HiMe model stack. Retention versus revision is not a distinction between HiMe and REMM: both can edit memory. REMM makes the supporting records and downstream withdrawal explicit."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The plotted ledger records the following assistance categories. Unrecorded does not mean unassisted. The two assisted REMM full completions are T1b (orange-block nudge) and T2 (help completing strawberry pickup). We preserve the recorded outcomes rather than silently reclassifying them."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"research-table-wrap","role":"region","aria-label":"Assistance fields in the 51-trial plotted ledger","tabIndex":0,"children":["$","$L24",null,{"className":"research-table","children":[["$","caption",null,{"children":"Assistance fields in the 51-trial plotted ledger"}],["$","$L25",null,{"children":["$","$L26",null,{"children":[["$","$L27","System",{"scope":"col","children":"System"}],["$","$L27","Recorded none",{"scope":"col","children":"Recorded none"}],["$","$L27","Task assistance",{"scope":"col","children":"Task assistance"}],["$","$L27","Unrecorded",{"scope":"col","children":"Unrecorded"}]]}]}],["$","$L28",null,{"children":[["$","$L26","0",{"className":"","children":[["$","$L27","0",{"scope":"row","children":"Vanilla G0.5"}],["$","$L29","1",{"children":"12"}],["$","$L29","2",{"children":"0"}],["$","$L29","3",{"children":"6"}]]}],["$","$L26","1",{"className":"","children":[["$","$L27","0",{"scope":"row","children":"HiMe adaptation"}],["$","$L29","1",{"children":"6"}],["$","$L29","2",{"children":"2"}],["$","$L29","3",{"children":"8"}]]}],["$","$L26","2",{"className":"ours-row","children":[["$","$L27","0",{"scope":"row","children":"REMM"}],["$","$L29","1",{"children":"10"}],["$","$L29","2",{"children":"4"}],["$","$L29","3",{"children":"3"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"prose","children":"A trial-level evidence audit is still needed before reporting an unassisted success rate or attributing the pooled gains to dependency propagation."}]]}]
